\begin{lemma}[Weak factorization in finitely many parameters]\label{lem:weak}
Suppose $G_0=G_1=G$. If $g\Gamma$ is not totally equidistributed on $[N]^k$,
it has a factorization (1) with $p$ in a standard proper connected rational
subgroup, retaining all conclusions of Theorem~\ref{thm:factor} except
the final equidistribution condition.
\end{lemma}

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:vertical}
For the descended integral character there is a finite-dimensional
unit-vector-valued smooth function on $\widetilde G/\widetilde\Gamma$ of
vertical frequency $\widetilde\eta$. Its dimension and Lipschitz bound depend
only on the fixed filtered group, lattice, metric and character.
\end{lemma}

